Package: qgctgan
Type: Package
Title: Quality-Aware Cluster-Conditioned Oversampling with Intra-Cluster
        Filtering
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Munil",
                  family = "Yang",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "miyang@ips.or.kr",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-1493-6691"))
Description: A generator-agnostic framework for oversampling imbalanced tabular
    data. The minority class is partitioned into sub-clusters with a Gaussian
    mixture model, synthetic candidates are drawn per sub-cluster from a
    pluggable generator, and the candidates pass a two-stage quality filter:
    a composite quality score combining intra-cluster density fidelity, class
    boundary separability and local-outlier behaviour with an adaptive
    per-cluster rejection quantile ('Stage 1'), followed by a greedy maximum
    mean discrepancy selection that aligns the retained synthetic set with the
    real minority distribution ('Stage 2'). A pure-R Gaussian generator is
    provided so the pipeline runs without external dependencies; an optional
    adapter calls a conditional tabular generative adversarial network through
    'reticulate' when higher-fidelity generation is required. Implements the
    method of Yang (2026, Applied Soft Computing).
